mpty geometries can be 3D, empty collections are always 2D\n    50\u2192\n    51\u2192    Parameters\n    52\u2192    ----------\n    53\u2192    geometry : Geometry or array_like\n    54\u2192        Geometry or geometries to convert to WKT.\n    55\u2192    rounding_precision : int, default 6\n    56\u2192        The rounding precision when writing the WKT string. Set to a value of\n    57\u2192        -1 to indicate the full precision.\n    58\u2192    trim : bool, default True\n    59\u2192        If True, trim unnecessary decimals (trailing zeros).\n    60\u2192    output_dimension : int, default None\n    61\u2192        The output dimension for the WKT string. Supported values are 2, 3 and\n    62\u2192        4 for GEOS 3.12+. Default None will automatically choose 3 or 4,\n    63\u2192        depending on the version of GEOS.\n    64\u2192        Specifying 3 means that up to 3 dimensions will be written but 2D\n    65\u2192        geometries will still be represented as 2D in the WKT string.\n    66\u2192    old_3d : bool, default False\n    67\u2192        Enable old style 3D/4D WKT generation. By default, new style 3D/4D WKT\n    68\u2192        (ie. \"POINT Z (10 20 30)\") is returned, but with ``old_3d=True``\n    69\u2192        the WKT will be formatted in the style \"POINT (10 20 30)\".\n    70\u2192    **kwargs\n    71\u2192        See :ref:`NumPy ufunc docs <ufuncs.kwargs>` for other keyword arguments.\n    72\u2192\n    73\u2192    Examples\n    74\u2192    --------\n    75\u2192    >>> from shapely import Point\n    76\u2192    >>> to_wkt(Point(0, 0))\n    77\u2192    'POINT (0 0)'\n    78\u2192    >>> to_wkt(Point(0, 0), rounding_precision=3, trim=False)\n    79\u2192    'POINT (0.000 0.000)'\n    80\u2192    >>> to_wkt(Point(0, 0), rounding_precision=-1, trim=False)\n    81\u2192    'POINT (0.0000000000000000 0.0000000000000000)'\n    82\u2192    >>> to_wkt(Point(1, 2, 3), trim=True)\n    83\u2192    'POINT Z (1 2 3)'\n    84\u2192    >>> to_w