ngeospatial.org/standards/sfs>`__.\n   131\u2192\n   132\u2192    The following limitations apply to WKB serialization:\n   133\u2192\n   134\u2192    - linearrings will be converted to linestrings\n   135\u2192    - a point with only NaN coordinates is converted to an empty point\n   136\u2192\n   137\u2192    Parameters\n   138\u2192    ----------\n   139\u2192    geometry : Geometry or array_like\n   140\u2192        Geometry or geometries to convert to WKB.\n   141\u2192    hex : bool, default False\n   142\u2192        If true, export the WKB as a hexadecimal string. The default is to\n   143\u2192        return a binary bytes object.\n   144\u2192    output_dimension : int, default None\n   145\u2192        The output dimension for the WKB. Supported values are 2, 3 and 4 for\n   146\u2192        GEOS 3.12+. Default None will automatically choose 3 or 4, depending on\n   147\u2192        the version of GEOS.\n   148\u2192        Specifying 3 means that up to 3 dimensions will be written but 2D\n   149\u2192        geometries will still be represented as 2D in the WKB representation.\n   150\u2192    byte_order : int, default -1\n   151\u2192        Defaults to native machine byte order (-1). Use 0 to force big endian\n   152\u2192        and 1 for little endian.\n   153\u2192    include_srid : bool, default False\n   154\u2192        If True, the SRID is be included in WKB (this is an extension\n   155\u2192        to the OGC WKB specification). Not allowed when flavor is \"iso\".\n   156\u2192    flavor : {\"iso\", \"extended\"}, default \"extended\"\n   157\u2192        Which flavor of WKB will be returned. The flavor determines how\n   158\u2192        extra dimensionality is encoded with the type number, and whether\n   159\u2192        SRID can be included in the WKB. ISO flavor is \"more standard\" for\n   160\u2192        3D output, and does not support SRID embedding.\n   161\u2192        Both flavors are equivalent when ``output_dimension=2`` (or with